title: 'statement-store: limit each retention track on its own'

doc:
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    On nodes running the v2 DHT statement path, the store now applies a separate count and size
    limit to the statements it keeps for DHT affinity, for explicit affinity alone, and to the
    transient ones it keeps only until propagated, on top of the global limits. Each limit defaults
    to the global one and is set with the hidden flags
    `--statement-store-max-{dht-affinity,explicit-affinity,transient}-{statements,size}`. The
    statement database migrates to version 3 on the first start, existing statements count as kept
    for DHT affinity.

crates:
- name: sc-statement-store
  bump: minor
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: minor
- name: staging-node-cli
  bump: patch
- name: polkadot-omni-node-lib
  bump: patch
